Article 89 The report on the ecological and environmental impact of a specific plan shall include the following:
(1) Analysis, prediction, and assessment of the possible impacts of implementing the plan on the ecological environment;
(2) Countermeasures and measures to prevent or mitigate adverse ecological and environmental impacts;
(3) Conclusion of the ecological and environmental impact assessment.

Article 95 The State shall implement classified management of ecological and environmental impact assessment of construction projects based on the degree of impact of the construction projects on the ecological environment.
The construction unit shall, in accordance with the following provisions, organize the preparation of an ecological and environmental impact report, an ecological and environmental impact report form, or fill out an ecological and environmental impact registration form:
(1) For projects that may cause significant ecological and environmental impacts, an ecological and environmental impact report shall be prepared to comprehensively evaluate the resulting ecological and environmental impacts;
(2) For projects that may cause minor ecological and environmental impacts, an ecological and environmental impact report form shall be prepared to analyze or conduct a specific evaluation of the resulting ecological and environmental impacts;
(3) For projects with minimal ecological and environmental impacts that do not require the preparation of an ecological and environmental impact report or report form, an ecological and environmental impact registration form shall be filled out.
The classified management catalogue for ecological and environmental impact assessment of construction projects shall be formulated and published by the competent department of ecology and environment of the State Council.

Article 96 An ecological and environmental impact report of a construction project shall include the following:
(1) Overview of the construction project;
(2) Current status of the ecological environment around the construction project;
(3) Analysis, prediction, and assessment of the possible impacts of the construction project on the ecological environment;
(4) Ecological and environmental protection measures for the construction project and their technical and economic feasibility;
(5) Economic cost-benefit analysis of the ecological and environmental impacts of the construction project;
(6) Recommendations for implementing ecological and environmental monitoring and discharge management for the construction project;
(7) Conclusion of the ecological and environmental impact assessment;
(8) Other contents as prescribed by law.
The content and format of the ecological and environmental impact report form and the ecological and environmental impact registration form shall be prescribed by the competent department of ecology and environment of the State Council.

Article 104 The competent ecological environmental department of the State Council shall be responsible for examining and approving the ecological environmental impact reports and ecological environmental impact statements of the following construction projects:
(1) Construction projects of special nature such as nuclear facilities;
(2) Construction projects that span the administrative regions of provinces, autonomous regions, or municipalities directly under the Central Government;
(3) Construction projects approved by the State Council or authorized by the State Council for approval by relevant departments;
(4) Other construction projects as provided by laws and administrative regulations.
The authority for examining and approving ecological environmental impact reports and ecological environmental impact statements of construction projects other than those specified in the preceding paragraph shall be prescribed by the people's governments of provinces, autonomous regions, or municipalities directly under the Central Government and shall be reported to the competent ecological environmental department of the State Council for filing.
If a construction project may cause adverse ecological environmental impacts across administrative regions, and the relevant competent ecological environmental departments have disputes over the conclusion of the ecological environmental impact assessment of the project, the ecological environmental impact report or the ecological environmental impact statement thereof shall be examined and approved by the common competent ecological environmental department at the next higher level.

Article 105 Where a construction project falls under any of the following circumstances, the competent ecological environmental department shall make a decision not to approve the ecological environmental impact report or the ecological environmental impact statement:
(1) The type, site selection, layout, and scale of the construction project do not comply with ecological environmental laws and regulations and relevant statutory plans;
(2) The ecological environmental quality of the area, river basin, or sea area where the project is located does not meet the ecological environmental quality standards, and the measures proposed by the construction project cannot meet the management requirements for ecological environmental quality improvement targets;
(3) The pollution prevention and control measures adopted by the construction project cannot ensure that pollutant emissions meet discharge standards, or necessary measures have not been taken to prevent and control ecological damage;
(4) For reconstruction, expansion, and technological transformation projects, effective prevention and control measures have not been proposed for the original environmental pollution and ecological damage of the project;
(5) The ecological environmental impact report or ecological environmental impact statement of the construction project has serious quality issues such as obviously false basic data, major defects, omissions, or falsehoods in content, or incorrect or unreasonable conclusions of ecological environmental impact assessment.

Article 176 The following enterprises, public institutions, and other business operators shall obtain an emission permit:
(1) Enterprises, public institutions, and coal-fired heat source production and operation units of centralized heating facilities that discharge industrial waste gas or toxic and hazardous air pollutants;
(2) Enterprises, public institutions, and other business operators that directly or indirectly discharge industrial wastewater or medical sewage into water bodies;
(3) Operation units of centralized urban sewage treatment facilities;
(4) Coastal engineering and marine engineering units that directly discharge industrial wastewater or medical sewage into the sea;
(5) Units that generate industrial solid waste;
(6) Enterprises, public institutions, and other business operators that discharge industrial noise;
(7) Units exploiting and utilizing associated radioactive mines that discharge radioactive waste liquid or generate radioactive solid waste;
(8) Enterprises and public institutions that operate Class I electromagnetic radiation facilities and enterprises and public institutions that operate Class II electromagnetic radiation facilities subject to emission permit management according to law;
(9) Other enterprises, public institutions, and other business operators subject to emission permit management in accordance with laws and administrative regulations.

Article 180 An emission permit shall be issued to enterprises, public institutions, and other business operators subject to emission permit management that meet the following conditions:
(1) They have lawfully obtained the approval documents for the environmental impact report and environmental impact statement, or have completed the filing procedures for the environmental impact registration form;
(2) Pollutant discharge meets the requirements of pollutant discharge standards, etc., and key pollutant discharge meets the requirements of the technical specifications for application and issuance of emission permits, the approval documents for the environmental impact report and environmental impact statement, and the total emission control indicators for key pollutants; if the business premises of enterprises, public institutions, and other business operators subject to emission permit management are located in areas, basins, or sea areas that have not met the national ecological and environmental quality standards, they shall also meet the special requirements of the relevant local people's governments on improving ecological and environmental quality;
(3) Using pollution prevention and control facilities can meet the requirements such as the permitted emission concentration, or comply with the available pollution prevention and control technologies;
(4) The monitoring points, indicators, frequency, etc. of the self-monitoring plan comply with the national self-monitoring specifications;
(5) Other conditions stipulated by laws and administrative regulations.

Article 181 A pollutant discharge permit shall contain the following information:
(1) The location and number of discharge outlets, the methods of pollutant discharge and the direction of discharge, etc.;
(2) The types of pollutants discharged, the permitted discharge concentration, the permitted discharge amount, or the permitted discharge limits, etc.;
(3) The links of generation and discharge of pollutants, the pollution prevention and control facilities and their operation and maintenance requirements, the standardization requirements for discharge outlets, etc.;
(4) The requirements for prohibiting or restricting the discharge of pollutants during special periods;
(5) Other information as prescribed by laws and administrative regulations.

Article 182 A pollutant discharge permit shall be valid for five years. Where any enterprise, public institution, or other producer or business operator that is subject to pollutant discharge permit management falls under any of the following circumstances within the validity period of the pollutant discharge permit, it shall obtain a new pollutant discharge permit:
(1) The construction of a new project, or the reconstruction or expansion of an existing project that discharges pollutants;
(2) Changes in the place of production or business operation, the location of the discharge outlet, or the method or direction of pollutant discharge;
(3) An increase in the number of discharge outlets or in the types, concentration, or amount of pollutants discharged;
(4) Other circumstances as prescribed by laws and administrative regulations.

Article 295 People's governments at all levels shall strengthen water pollution prevention and control, and allocate necessary funds for the following matters:
(1) Scientific and technological research and development, demonstration projects, and programs for water pollution prevention and control;
(2) Activities organized and implemented by people's governments at all levels and their relevant departments, such as investigation and assessment of water ecological environment conditions, watershed water pollution treatment, protection of centralized drinking water sources, construction and maintenance of urban sewage treatment pipe networks, investigation and remediation of sewage outlets into rivers, treatment of black and odorous water bodies, ecological environmental protection of groundwater, and capacity building for supervision and management of water pollution prevention and control;
(3) Emergency response by people's governments at all levels and their relevant departments to water pollution accidents;
(4) Other matters related to water pollution prevention and control as prescribed by people's governments at all levels.

Article 332: For characteristic industries and unique pollutants for which there are no national water pollutant discharge standards, as well as specific water pollution sources or water pollutants for which the state has clear requirements, the people's governments of provinces, autonomous regions, and municipalities directly under the Central Government in key river basins shall supplement local water pollutant discharge standards and report them to the competent department of ecology and environment of the State Council for recordation.
In any of the following circumstances, the people's governments of provinces, autonomous regions, and municipalities directly under the Central Government in key river basins shall formulate local water pollutant discharge standards that are stricter than the national water pollutant discharge standards, and report them to the competent department of ecology and environment of the State Council for recordation:
(1) The industry is intensive and the problem of water environmental pollution is prominent;
(2) The existing water pollutant discharge standards cannot meet the water ecological environment quality requirements of the key river basin;
(3) The water ecological environment situation of the river basin or region is complex, making it impossible to apply uniform water pollutant discharge standards.

Article 403 The competent departments of agriculture and rural affairs and forestry and grassland of local people's governments shall, jointly with the competent departments of ecological environment and natural resources, conduct focused monitoring on the following agricultural land plots:
(1) Where the pollutant content in the agricultural products produced exceeds the standard;
(2) Which serve or have served as sewage irrigation areas;
(3) Which are or have been used for large-scale farming, or for the stacking or landfill of solid waste;
(4) Which have been used as industrial or mining land, or where major or extraordinarily major pollution accidents have occurred;
(5) Which are in the vicinity of facilities for the production, storage, utilization, or disposal of toxic and hazardous substances; and
(6) Other circumstances specified by the competent departments of agriculture and rural affairs, forestry and grassland, ecological environment, and natural resources of the State Council.

Article 404 The competent department of ecological environment of a local people's government shall, jointly with the competent department of natural resources, conduct focused monitoring on the following construction land plots:
(1) Which have been used for the production, storage, use, recovery, or disposal of toxic and hazardous substances;
(2) Which have been used for the stacking or landfill of solid waste;
(3) Where major or extraordinarily major pollution accidents have occurred; and
(4) Other circumstances specified by the competent departments of ecological environment and natural resources of the State Council.

Article 409 People's governments at all levels shall strengthen soil pollution prevention and control and allocate necessary funds for the following matters:
(1) Scientific and technological research and development, demonstration projects, and programs on soil pollution prevention and control;
(2) Activities organized and implemented by people's governments at all levels and their relevant departments, including soil pollution surveys, monitoring, investigations, identification of persons responsible for soil pollution, risk assessment, risk control, remediation, and the like;
(3) Emergency response by people's governments at all levels and their relevant departments to sudden incidents involving soil pollution; and
(4) Other matters concerning soil pollution prevention and control as prescribed by people's governments at all levels.

Article 423 The State encourages and supports agricultural producers and operators to adopt the following measures:
(1) use high-efficiency, low-toxicity and low-residue pesticides and advanced spraying technologies;
(2) use organic fertilizers and high-efficiency fertilizers that meet the standards;
(3) adopt soil testing and formulated fertilization technologies, and green prevention and control technologies for diseases, pests and weeds such as biological control;
(4) use biodegradable agricultural films;
(5) comprehensively utilize straw and remove straw with high enrichment of pollutants; and
(6) improve degraded soil, etc. according to the provisions.

Article 432 When conducting a soil pollution risk assessment, a soil pollution risk assessment report shall be prepared.
The soil pollution risk assessment report shall mainly include the following:
(1) the status of the main pollutants;
(2) the scope of soil and groundwater pollution;
(3) risks to the quality and safety of agricultural products, risks to public health or risks to the ecological environment; and
(4) the objectives and basic requirements for risk control and remediation, etc.

Article 448 For agricultural land plots of safe utilization class, the competent departments of agricultural and rural affairs and of forestry and grassland of the local people's government shall, within their respective functions and duties, formulate and implement a safe utilization plan based on the main crop varieties and cultivation habits and other circumstances.
The safe utilization plan shall include the following contents:
(1) agronomic regulation and alternative planting;
(2) regular collaborative monitoring and evaluation of soil and agricultural products;
(3) technical guidance and training for farmers, farmer specialized cooperatives, and other agricultural production and business entities;
(4) other risk control measures.

Article 449 For agricultural land plots of strict control class, the competent departments of agricultural and rural affairs and of forestry and grassland of the local people's government shall, within their respective functions and duties, take the following risk control measures:
(1) propose to designate areas where the production of specific agricultural products is prohibited, and implement after reporting to and obtaining approval from the people's government at the same level;
(2) conduct collaborative monitoring and evaluation of soil and agricultural products in accordance with the provisions;
(3) provide technical guidance and training for farmers, farmer specialized cooperatives, and other agricultural production and business entities;
(4) other risk control measures.
People's governments at all levels and their relevant departments shall encourage the adoption of risk control measures such as adjusting planting structure, returning farmland to forest or grassland, returning farmland to wetland, crop rotation and fallowing, and rotational grazing and rest grazing for strict control class agricultural land, and provide corresponding policy support.

Article 458 For plots in the list for risk control and remediation of soil contamination on construction land, the competent department of ecological environment of the local people's government may, based on the actual circumstances, take the following risk control measures:
(1) propose to designate isolation areas, and implement after reporting to and obtaining approval from the people's government at the same level;
(2) monitor the status of soil and groundwater contamination;
(3) other risk control measures.

Article 483 People's governments at all levels shall strengthen the prevention and control of solid waste pollution and allocate necessary funds for the following matters:
(1) scientific and technological research and development for the prevention and control of solid waste pollution;
(2) classification of domestic waste;
(3) construction of facilities for the storage, utilization, and centralized disposal of solid waste;
(4) emergency disposal of hazardous waste, such as medical waste generated by emergencies like major infectious disease outbreaks; and
(5) other matters related to the prevention and control of solid waste pollution as prescribed by people's governments at all levels.

The State implements a qualification management system for professionals engaged in the prevention and control of radioactive pollution, and a qualification management system for institutions engaged in the monitoring of radioactive pollution.
Institutions engaged in the monitoring of radioactive pollution shall meet the following conditions and, after being lawfully examined and certified qualified by the competent department of ecological environment under the State Council and obtaining a qualification certificate, may engage in the monitoring of radioactive pollution within the scope of the qualification license:
(1) have legal person status;
(2) have professional and technical personnel matching the monitoring work;
(3) have workplaces, experimental conditions, facilities and equipment meeting the requirements of relevant standards and specifications;
(4) have a sound quality management system.

Article 730 The following acts that damage wetlands and their ecological functions are prohibited:
(1) Reclaiming (enclosing) or draining natural wetlands, or permanently cutting off water sources of natural wetlands;
(2) Unauthorized filling of natural wetlands, unauthorized sand extraction, mining, or earth taking;
(3) Discharging industrial wastewater, domestic sewage, or other waste water or sewage that pollutes wetlands that do not meet the discharge standards for water pollutants, or dumping, piling up, discarding, scattering, or spilling solid waste;
(4) Overgrazing or indiscriminate gathering of wild plants, overfishing or exterminatory fishing, excessive fertilization, application of chemicals, baiting, or other planting or breeding activities that pollute wetlands;
(5) Other acts that damage wetlands and their ecological functions.
No trees growing on wetlands shall be felled without authorization; if felling is truly necessary, a felling permit shall be obtained according to law.

Article 905: The State encourages and supports the adoption of the following measures conducive to soil and water conservation in mountainous areas, hilly areas, wind-sand areas and other areas prone to soil erosion:
(1) no-tillage, contour farming, rotational tillage and cropping, grass-crop rotation, intercropping and interplanting, etc.;
(2) closure and tending, rotational enclosure and grazing, and stall feeding and pen raising;
(3) developing biomass energy, utilizing solar energy, wind energy and hydro energy, replacing firewood with coal, electricity and gas, etc.;
(4) relocating people outward from ecologically fragile areas; and
(5) other measures conducive to soil and water conservation.

Article 965 In the process of technological transformation, an enterprise shall adopt the following clean production measures:
(1) adopting non-toxic, harmless or low-toxicity, low-harm raw materials to replace raw materials with high toxicity and serious hazards;
(2) adopting processes and equipment with high resource utilization rates and low generation of pollutants and greenhouse gases to replace processes and equipment with low resource utilization rates and high generation of pollutants and greenhouse gases;
(3) comprehensively utilizing wastes generated during the production process;
(4) adopting pollution prevention and control technologies that can meet the pollutant discharge standards and the total pollutant discharge control targets prescribed by the State or local authorities.

Article 1059 If pollution of the environment or damage to the ecosystem is caused by force majeure, no compensation liability shall be borne, unless otherwise provided by law. If pollution damage is caused to the marine environment, the provisions of paragraph 3 of this Article shall apply.
If the damage is caused intentionally by the victim, the relevant liable person shall not bear compensation liability; if the damage is caused by gross negligence of the victim, the compensation liability may be mitigated.
If it falls entirely under any of the following circumstances and, after timely taking reasonable measures, pollution damage to the marine environment still cannot be avoided, the relevant liable person causing the pollution damage shall be exempted from liability:
(1) War;
(2) Irresistible natural disasters;
(3) Negligence or other wrongful acts of the competent authority responsible for lighthouses or other navigation aids in the performance of its duties.

Article 1062 Where local people's governments at all levels, departments, and institutions responsible for ecological and environmental protection supervision and administration are under any of the following circumstances, the leading persons with responsibility and the directly responsible persons shall be given a demerit, a major demerit, or a demotion sanction; if serious consequences are caused, they shall be given a removal from office or expulsion sanction:
(1) failing to grant an administrative license or handle approval documents according to law;
(2) covering up illegal eco-environmental acts;
(3) failing to make a decision ordering suspension of business or closure as legally required;
(4) upon discovery or receipt of a report, failing to timely investigate and handle according to law acts such as discharging pollutants not in accordance with permit provisions, discharging pollutants by means evading supervision, causing environmental pollution or ecological damage accidents, and failing to implement ecological protection measures resulting in ecological damage;
(5) illegally sealing up or impounding relevant premises, vessels, installations, equipment, tools, or articles of enterprises, institutions, and other producers and business operators;
(6) falsifying, forging, or instructing the falsification or forgery of monitoring data;
(7) failing to disclose eco-environmental information that shall be disclosed according to law;
(8) illegally collecting fees, or intercepting, misappropriating, or diverting fees collected according to law for other purposes;
(9) failing to transfer according to law a case that shall be transferred to a relevant organ for handling;
(10) other illegal circumstances as provided for by laws and regulations.

Article 1081: The organ or organization that files a lawsuit with the People's Court pursuant to Articles 1073 and 1075 of this Law shall provide the following evidence:
(1) the act of the perpetrator polluting the environment or damaging the ecosystem;
(2) the act violates the provisions of the law;
(3) the circumstances of ecological and environmental damage;
(4) the costs of ecological and environmental losses, the costs of ecological and environmental restoration, and other costs;
(5) other matters that shall be evidenced.
Where a lawsuit is filed pursuant to Article 1074 of this Law, the evidence specified in items (1), (3) to (5) of the preceding paragraph shall be provided.

Article 1086: Where any provision of this Law is violated and any of the following circumstances exists, the department or institution responsible for ecological and environmental protection supervision and administration shall, according to its division of duties, order correction and impose a fine of not less than 20,000 yuan but not more than 200,000 yuan; if the party refuses to correct, it may order restricted production or suspension of operations for remediation:
(1) failure to conduct self-monitoring of the pollutants discharged, aquaculture tail water, or soil pollution status, failure to formulate a self-monitoring plan, failure to establish management ledgers, failure to preserve original monitoring records and management ledgers, and failure to report truthfully;
(2) failure to install, use, maintain, or operate normally automatic pollutant discharge monitoring and surveillance equipment, failure to connect with the competent department's surveillance equipment, failure to preserve original monitoring records, and failure to report truthfully;
(3) failure to monitor the discharge outlets of toxic and hazardous pollutants and the surrounding environment, and failure to disclose information on toxic and hazardous pollutants.
Where a provision of this Law is violated and a domestic waste treatment unit fails to install or use pollutant discharge monitoring equipment, conduct real-time monitoring of pollutant discharge, and disclose pollutant discharge data, the competent department of ecology and environment shall order correction and impose a fine of not less than 50,000 yuan but not more than 500,000 yuan; if the party refuses to correct, a fine of not less than 500,000 yuan but not more than 1,000,000 yuan shall be imposed.

Article 1114: Where, in violation of this Law, any of the following circumstances exists, the competent energy department shall order rectification and impose a fine of not less than 100,000 yuan but not more than 1,000,000 yuan; if rectification is refused, the matter shall be reported to the people's government with the power of approval for approval, and an order to suspend business or close down shall be issued:
(1) A coal mine fails to construct supporting coal washing and dressing facilities;
(2) A coal-fired power plant or other coal-burning unit fails to construct supporting dust removal, desulfurization, denitrification and other devices, or fails to adopt technical renovation or other measures to control the discharge of air pollutants;
(3) An enterprise such as steel, building materials, non-ferrous metals, petroleum, or chemical engineering that emits dust, sulfides, and nitrogen oxides during the production process fails to construct supporting dust removal, desulfurization, denitrification and other devices, or fails to adopt technical renovation or other measures to control the discharge of air pollutants.
Where, in violation of this Law, coal containing toxic and hazardous substances such as radioactive substances and arsenic exceeding the prescribed standards is mined, the people's government at or above the county level shall, in accordance with the authority prescribed by the State Council, order suspension of business or close down.

Article 1115: Where, in violation of this Law, any of the following circumstances exists, the market supervision and administration department shall order rectification, confiscate the raw materials, products, and illegal gains, and impose a fine of not less than one time but not more than five times the value of the goods:
(1) Selling coal or petroleum coke that does not meet the quality standards;
(2) Selling high-pollution fuel within a prohibited burning area;
(3) Producing or selling raw and auxiliary materials or products whose volatile organic compound content does not meet the quality standards or requirements;
(4) Producing or selling fuels, engine oils, nitrogen oxide reducing agents, fuel and lubricant additives, and other additives for motor vehicles, vessels, and non-road mobile machinery that do not meet the standards.

Article 1116: Where, in violation of this Law, any of the following circumstances exists, the Customs shall order the return of the goods, confiscate the illegal gains, and impose a fine of not less than one time but not more than five times the value of the goods; if the goods cannot be returned, the raw materials and products shall be confiscated:
(1) Importing coal or petroleum coke that does not meet the quality standards;
(2) Importing raw and auxiliary materials or products whose volatile organic compound content does not meet the quality standards or requirements;
(3) Importing fuels, engine oils, nitrogen oxide reducing agents, fuel and lubricant additives, and other additives for motor vehicles, vessels, and non-road mobile machinery that do not meet the standards.

Article 1119: Where, in violation of this Law, any of the following circumstances exists, the competent department of ecological environment shall confiscate the facilities using high-pollution fuel and the coal-fired heating boilers and organize their dismantling, and impose a fine of not less than 20,000 yuan but not more than 200,000 yuan:
(1) Constructing or expanding facilities using high-pollution fuel within a prohibited burning area;
(2) Failing to stop using high-pollution fuel within a prohibited burning area;
(3) Constructing or expanding decentralized coal-fired heating boilers in areas covered by urban centralized heating pipe networks;
(4) Failing to dismantle existing coal-fired heating boilers that cannot meet the discharge standards within the required time limit.
Where, in violation of this Law, boilers that do not meet the prescribed standards or requirements are produced, imported, or sold, the market supervision and administration department shall order rectification, confiscate the illegal gains, and impose a fine of not less than 20,000 yuan but not more than 200,000 yuan; where boilers that do not meet the prescribed standards or requirements are used, the competent department of ecological environment shall order rectification, confiscate the illegal gains, and impose a fine of not less than 20,000 yuan but not more than 200,000 yuan.

Article 1120: Where, in violation of this Law, any of the following circumstances exists, the competent department of ecological environment shall order rectification and impose a fine of not less than 20,000 yuan but not more than 200,000 yuan; if rectification is refused, suspension of production for remediation shall be ordered:
(1) An industrial painting enterprise, etc., fails to use raw and auxiliary materials or products with low volatile organic compound content;
(2) Raw and auxiliary materials or products that generate volatile organic compounds are produced or used without being carried out in a closed space or equipment and without installing and using pollution prevention and control facilities or taking measures to reduce waste gas emissions;
(3) Enterprises such as petroleum, chemical engineering, and other enterprises that produce and use organic solvents fail to take measures for daily maintenance and repair of pipes and equipment, or fail to collect and treat leaked materials in a timely manner;
(4) Oil storage depots, gas stations, tanker trucks, etc., fail to install and properly use oil and gas recovery devices in accordance with state regulations;
(5) Enterprises such as steel, building materials, non-ferrous metals, petroleum, chemical engineering, pharmaceutical, mining, and other industrial production enterprises fail to take measures such as centralized collection and treatment, enclosure, shielding, covering, sweeping, and water spraying to control and reduce the emission of dust and gaseous pollutants;
(6) Combustible gases generated from industrial production, landfill, or other activities are not recovered or utilized, and where recovery and utilization conditions are not available, no pollution prevention and control treatment is carried out;
(7) A combustible gas recovery and utilization device fails to operate normally and is not repaired or replaced in a timely manner;
(8) Combustible gases are discharged during the period when the combustible gas recovery and utilization device cannot operate normally, without taking measures to control the discharge of air pollutants.
Where, in violation of this Law, crude oil and refined oil terminals, crude oil and refined oil transport vessels, or railway tank cars fail to install and properly use oil and gas recovery devices in accordance with state regulations, the competent departments of ecological environment, transportation, maritime administration, etc., shall, in accordance with the division of duties, impose penalties in accordance with the preceding paragraph.

Article 1130: Where, in violation of this Law, any of the following circumstances occurs, the departments of ecological environment, among others, shall, according to their respective responsibilities, order correction and impose a fine of not less than 10,000 yuan but not more than 100,000 yuan; if the party refuses to correct, it shall order suspension of work for remediation or suspension of business for remediation:
(1) When loading or unloading materials, sealing or spraying methods are not adopted to prevent dust pollution;
(2) Materials prone to generating dust such as coal, coal gangue, coal slag, coal ash, cement, lime, gypsum, sand, iron ore, etc., are not stored in a sealed manner;
(3) For materials prone to generating dust that cannot be stored in a sealed manner, a tight enclosure not lower than the height of the stockpile is not set up, or effective covering measures are not taken to prevent dust pollution;
(4) An entity stores coal, coal gangue, coal slag, coal ash, and other materials without taking fire prevention measures;
(5) Docks, mines, landfills, and receiving sites do not carry out partitioned operations or take effective measures to prevent dust pollution;
(6) Enterprises or institutions discharging toxic and hazardous air pollutants listed in the catalogue of toxic and hazardous air pollutants fail to establish an environmental risk early warning system, investigate environmental safety hazards, and take effective measures to prevent environmental risks;
(7) Enterprises, institutions, or other production or business operators that discharge persistent organic pollutants into the atmosphere, or operators of waste incineration facilities, fail to adopt technical methods and processes that help reduce the emission of persistent organic pollutants or to equip with effective purification devices;
(8) Effective measures are not taken to prevent the emission of malodorous gases.

Article 1136: Where, in violation of this Law, any of the following circumstances occurs, the competent department of ecological environment shall order cessation of the illegal act, take control measures to eliminate pollution, impose a fine, and may order measures such as restricted production and suspension of operations for remediation; if the party refuses to take control measures, the department may designate a unit with the capability to carry out the remediation on its behalf, with the costs borne by the violator; if the circumstances are serious, the matter shall be reported to the people's government with approval authority for approval to order suspension of business and closure:
(1) Discharging oils, acid solutions, or alkali solutions into waters;
(2) Discharging highly toxic waste liquids into waters, or discharging, dumping, or directly burying soluble highly toxic waste residues containing mercury, cadmium, arsenic, chromium, lead, cyanide, yellow phosphorus, etc., into waters;
(3) Cleaning vehicles or containers that have stored oils or toxic or hazardous pollutants in waters;
(4) Discharging thermal wastewater or wastewater containing pathogens into waters in violation of state regulations or standards;
(5) Discharging or dumping industrial waste residues, municipal garbage, or other waste into waters, or dumping, piling up, or storing solid waste or other pollutants into rivers, lakes, canals, channels, reservoirs, and their beaches and bank slopes below the highest water level, or other locations prescribed by laws and regulations.
Where any of the circumstances specified in items (3) or (4) of the preceding paragraph occurs, a fine of not less than 20,000 yuan but not more than 200,000 yuan shall be imposed; where any of the circumstances specified in items (1) or (5) of the preceding paragraph occurs, a fine of not less than 100,000 yuan but not more than 1,000,000 yuan shall be imposed; where the circumstance specified in item (2) of the preceding paragraph occurs, a fine of not less than 200,000 yuan but not more than 2,000,000 yuan shall be imposed.

Article 1137: Where, in violation of this Law, any of the following circumstances occurs, the competent department of ecological environment shall order cessation of the illegal act, take control measures to eliminate pollution, impose a fine, and may order measures such as restricted production and suspension of operations for remediation; if the party refuses to take control measures, the department shall designate a unit with the capability to carry out the remediation on its behalf, with the costs borne by the violator; if the circumstances are serious, the matter shall be reported to the people's government with approval authority for approval to order suspension of business and closure:
(1) Failure to take anti-leakage measures or to construct groundwater quality monitoring wells for monitoring;
(2) Underground oil tanks at gas stations, oil extraction plants, etc., are not double-walled or other effective measures such as constructing anti-leakage pools are not taken, or anti-leakage monitoring is not conducted;
(3) Using ditches, pits, or ponds without anti-leakage measures to transport or store wastewater containing toxic or hazardous pollutants, wastewater containing pathogens, or other waste;
(4) Failure to take protective measures as required.
Where any of the circumstances specified in items (1) or (2) of the preceding paragraph occurs, a fine of not less than 20,000 yuan but not more than 200,000 yuan shall be imposed; where any of the circumstances specified in items (3) or (4) of the preceding paragraph occurs, a fine of not less than 100,000 yuan but not more than 1,000,000 yuan shall be imposed.

Article 1139: Where, in violation of this Law, any of the following circumstances occurs, the competent department of ecological environment shall order correction, impose a fine, and may order measures such as restricted production and suspension of operations for remediation; if the circumstances are serious, the matter shall be reported to the people's government with approval authority for approval to order suspension of business and closure:
(1) Failure to take effective measures, resulting in the direct discharge into waters of fire-fighting waste generated during the handling of production safety accidents that may seriously pollute waters;
(2) Diluting and discharging industrial wastewater containing toxic or hazardous water pollutants, but which does not constitute discharging pollutants by means of evading supervision;
(3) Discharging industrial wastewater or medical wastewater into farmland irrigation channels;
(4) Discharging urban wastewater and aquaculture tail water not utilized comprehensively, or agro-product processing wastewater into farmland irrigation channels, causing the water quality at the nearest irrigation intake downstream to fail to meet the water quality standards for farmland irrigation.
Where any of the circumstances specified in items (3) or (4) of the preceding paragraph occurs, a fine of not less than 20,000 yuan but not more than 200,000 yuan shall be imposed; where any of the circumstances specified in items (1) or (2) of the preceding paragraph occurs, a fine of not less than 100,000 yuan but not more than 1,000,000 yuan shall be imposed.

第一千一百四十三条 Any person who, in violation of this Law, commits any of the following acts shall be ordered to cease the illegal act by the maritime administrative agency or the fishery and fishery administration department according to their respective functions and duties, and shall be fined not less than 10,000 yuan but not more than 100,000 yuan; if water pollution is caused, the person shall be ordered to take control measures within a specified time limit to eliminate the pollution, and shall be fined not less than 20,000 yuan but not more than 200,000 yuan; if the control measures are not taken within the specified time limit, a unit with the ability to control shall be designated to carry out the control on behalf of the violator, and the expenses incurred shall be borne by the ship:
(1) Dumping garbage into waters or discharging residual oil, waste oil, oily wastewater, or domestic sewage from a ship;
(2) Loading and transporting oil or toxic and hazardous goods without taking measures to prevent overflow and leakage;
(3) Engaging in operational activities with pollution risks without taking pollution prevention and control measures;
(4) Conducting lightering operations of bulk liquid pollution-hazardous cargo without preparing a plan or without reporting for approval according to regulations.

Any person who, in violation of this Law, carries out ship scrapping operations by beaching shall be ordered to cease the illegal act by the maritime administrative agency or the fishery and fishery administration department according to their respective functions and duties, and shall be fined not less than 100,000 yuan but not more than 1,000,000 yuan.

Any international voyage ship entering the inland waters of the People's Republic of China that, in violation of this Law, discharges ship ballast water that does not comply with the regulations shall be ordered to cease the illegal act by the maritime administrative agency or the fishery and fishery administration department according to their respective functions and duties, and shall be fined not less than 20,000 yuan but not more than 200,000 yuan.

第一千一百四十四条 Any person who, in violation of this Law, commits any of the following acts shall be ordered to make corrections by the maritime administrative agency or the fishery and fishery administration department according to their respective functions and duties, and shall be fined not less than 20,000 yuan but not more than 200,000 yuan:
(1) A port, wharf, loading and unloading station, or shipbuilding and repairing yard fails to be equipped with or effectively operate facilities for receiving ship pollutants and wastes according to regulations;
(2) Engaging in the reception of ship pollutants and wastes or tank cleaning operations without having the corresponding reception and treatment capacity.

第一千一百四十五条 Any person who, in violation of this Law, commits any of the following acts shall be ordered to cease the illegal act by the competent department of ecological environment, shall be fined not less than 100,000 yuan but not more than 500,000 yuan, and shall be ordered to demolish or close down upon approval by the people's government with the approval authority:
(1) Constructing, rebuilding, or expanding a construction project unrelated to water supply facilities and the protection of the water source in a first-class protection zone of a drinking water source;
(2) Constructing, rebuilding, or expanding a construction project that discharges pollutants in a second-class protection zone of a drinking water source;
(3) Constructing or expanding a construction project that seriously pollutes the water body in a quasi-protection zone of a drinking water source, or rebuilding a construction project to increase the amount of pollutant discharge.

Any person who, in violation of this Law, engages in cage culture or organizes tourism, angling, or other activities that may pollute the drinking water body in a first-class protection zone of a drinking water source shall be ordered to cease the illegal act by the competent department of ecological environment, and shall be fined not less than 20,000 yuan but not more than 100,000 yuan. An individual who swims, angles, or engages in other activities that may pollute the drinking water body in a first-class protection zone of a drinking water source shall be ordered to cease the illegal act by the competent department of ecological environment, and may be fined not more than 500 yuan.

Any drinking water supply unit that, in violation of this Law, supplies water with quality that does not meet the national standards shall be ordered to make corrections by the competent water supply department, and shall be fined not less than 20,000 yuan but not more than 200,000 yuan; if the circumstances are serious, it may be ordered to suspend operations for rectification upon approval by the people's government with the approval authority.

第一千一百四十七条 Any person who, in violation of this Law, commits any of the following acts shall be ordered to make corrections by the departments and agencies with the functions and duties of ecological and environmental protection supervision and management according to their respective functions and duties, shall be fined, and may be ordered to take measures such as restricting production or suspending production for remediation; if the circumstances are serious, the person shall be ordered to suspend operations or close down upon approval by the people's government with the approval authority:
(1) Discharging oil, acid, or alkaline liquid into the sea;
(2) Discharging residual oil or waste oil from offshore oil and gas equipment into the sea;
(3) Discharging highly toxic waste liquid into the sea;
(4) Discharging oil-based mud and other toxic composite mud used in drilling into the sea;
(5) Discharging oily wastewater or oily mixtures that do not meet the standards into the sea;
(6) Disposing of oil-containing industrial solid waste into the sea;
(7) Discharging, in violation of national regulations or standards, heated wastewater, medical wastewater, domestic sewage, or industrial wastewater containing pathogens, or wastewater containing non-biodegradable organic substances or heavy metals into the sea;
(8) Discarding, piling, or treating solid waste on the shore or beach.

For any of the circumstances in the preceding paragraph except item (3), a fine of not less than 100,000 yuan but not more than 1,000,000 yuan shall be imposed; for the circumstance in item (3) of the preceding paragraph, a fine of not less than 200,000 yuan but not more than 2,000,000 yuan shall be imposed.

If an individual, without authorization, discards, piles, or treats domestic waste on the shore or beach, a fine of not less than 100 yuan but not more than 1,000 yuan shall be imposed per instance.

第一千一百四十八条 Any person engaged in mariculture activities who, in violation of this Law, commits any of the following acts shall be ordered to make corrections by the departments and agencies with the functions and duties of ecological and environmental protection supervision and management according to their respective functions and duties, and shall be fined not less than 5,000 yuan but not more than 50,000 yuan; if the circumstances are serious, the person shall be fined not less than 50,000 yuan but not more than 200,000 yuan, and shall be ordered to suspend operations or close down upon approval by the people's government with the approval authority:
(1) Violating the regulations on the scale and density of mariculture;
(2) Violating the regulations on bait, fertilizer, feed, or drug application.

第一千一百五十条 Any coastal engineering or marine engineering construction project that, in violation of this Law, commits any of the following acts shall be ordered to cease the illegal act and eliminate the hazard by the departments and agencies with the functions and duties of ecological and environmental protection supervision and management according to their respective functions and duties, and shall be fined not less than 200,000 yuan but not more than 1,000,000 yuan; if the circumstances are serious, the project shall be ordered to suspend operations or close down upon approval by the people's government with the approval authority:
(1) Using materials containing radioactive substances exceeding the standard or toxic and hazardous substances that are easily leachable;
(2) Causing erosion, silting, or damage to the baseline points of the territorial sea and their surrounding environment;
(3) Endangering the stability of the baseline points of the territorial sea.

第一千一百五十二条 Any person who, in violation of this Law, commits any of the following acts shall be ordered to make corrections by the competent department of ecological environment of the State Council and its regional sea agencies, the maritime administrative agency, or the maritime police agency according to their respective functions and duties, shall be fined, the dumping permit shall be temporarily seized or revoked, and if necessary, the ship may be detained; if the circumstances are serious, the person shall be ordered to suspend operations or close down upon approval by the people's government with the approval authority:
(1) Dumping waste into the sea without obtaining a dumping permit;
(2) Dumping waste not in accordance with the provisions of the dumping permit;
(3) Failing to install and use online monitoring equipment for marine dumping that meets requirements and connect it with the supervision system;
(4) Failing to report dumping circumstances according to regulations;
(5) A ship that dumps waste departing from port without reporting;
(6) A unit that has been approved to dump waste failing to entrust or supervise the implementation of marine waste dumping operations in accordance with this Law;
(7) Incinerating waste at sea.

For the circumstance in item (5) of the preceding paragraph, the owner, operator, or manager of the illegal ship shall be fined not less than 3,000 yuan but not more than 30,000 yuan, and the captain, responsible crew members, or other responsible persons shall be fined not less than 500 yuan but not more than 5,000 yuan; for the circumstance in item (4) of the preceding paragraph, a fine of not less than 5,000 yuan but not more than 20,000 yuan shall be imposed per instance; for the circumstance in item (3) of the preceding paragraph, a fine of not less than 20,000 yuan but not more than 200,000 yuan shall be imposed; for the circumstance in item (6) of the preceding paragraph, a fine of not less than 30,000 yuan but not more than 300,000 yuan shall be imposed; for the circumstance in item (1) of the preceding paragraph, a fine of not less than 200,000 yuan but not more than 2,000,000 yuan shall be imposed; for the circumstance in item (7) of the preceding paragraph, a fine of not less than 500,000 yuan but not more than 5,000,000 yuan shall be imposed. If any of the circumstances in items (1) or (7) of the preceding paragraph occurs and the person has been subject to administrative penalties three or more times within two years, the person shall not engage in marine waste dumping activities for three years; for the circumstance in item (2) of the preceding paragraph, a fine of not less than 200,000 yuan but not more than 1,000,000 yuan shall be imposed, and if the dumping permit is revoked, the person shall not engage in marine waste dumping activities for three years.

Any person who, in violation of this Law, obtains a dumping permit by fraudulent or bribery means or other improper means shall have the dumping permit revoked according to law by the competent department of ecological environment of the State Council or its regional sea agencies, and shall be fined not less than 200,000 yuan but not more than 500,000 yuan; and the person shall not apply for a dumping permit again within three years.

第一千一百五十三条 Any person who, in violation of this Law, commits any of the following acts shall be ordered to make corrections by the departments and agencies with the functions and duties of ecological and environmental protection supervision and management according to their respective functions and duties, and shall be fined:
(1) A ship discharging pollutants, wastes, or other harmful substances such as ship garbage, domestic sewage, oily wastewater, wastewater containing toxic and hazardous substances, or exhaust gas into the sea;
(2) Discharging ship ballast water and sediment that do not comply with regulations into the sea;
(3) A ship carrying pollution-hazardous goods entering or leaving a port or loading or unloading without approval;
(4) A ship conducting lightering operations of bulk liquid pollution-hazardous goods without preparing an operational plan or without reporting for approval according to regulations;
(5) During the loading and unloading of oil and toxic and hazardous goods, the ship and shore parties failing to comply with safety and anti-pollution operational procedures.

For any of the circumstances in items (2) to (5) of the preceding paragraph, a fine of not less than 20,000 yuan but not more than 100,000 yuan shall be imposed; for the circumstance in item (1) of the preceding paragraph, a fine of not less than 100,000 yuan but not more than 500,000 yuan shall be imposed.

第一千一百五十四条 Any person who, in violation of this Law, commits any of the following acts shall be ordered to make corrections by the departments and agencies with the functions and duties of ecological and environmental protection supervision and management according to their respective functions and duties, and shall be fined:
(1) The materials, structure, or anti-pollution equipment and facilities of a ship do not comply with the national regulations on the prevention and control of marine environment pollution from ships, or have not passed inspection;
(2) A ship does not hold certificates or documents for the prevention and control of marine environment pollution;
(3) A ship, in the discharge or operation involving ship pollutants, ballast water, and sediment, fails to conduct monitoring and surveillance according to regulations, or fails to truthfully record and preserve the relevant information;
(4) A ship fails to carry a list of hazardous materials on board, fails to continuously update the list of hazardous materials during the ship's construction, operation, and repair, or fails to provide the list of hazardous materials to the unit engaged in ship scrapping before scrapping;
(5) A ship taking measures to improve energy efficiency fails to meet the relevant requirements;
(6) A ship entering a ship pollutant emission control area does not comply with the relevant control requirements for ship pollutant emissions;
(7) A ship with shore power connection conditions, when berthing, fails to use shore power in accordance with national regulations;
(8) A port operator or shore power supply enterprise with the capacity to supply shore power fails to provide shore power to ships with shore power connection conditions in accordance with national regulations.

For the circumstance in item (4) of the preceding paragraph, a fine of not more than 20,000 yuan shall be imposed; for any of the circumstances in items (1) or (2) of the preceding paragraph, a fine of not less than 10,000 yuan but not more than 100,000 yuan shall be imposed, and if correction is refused, the ship shall be ordered to suspend navigation temporarily; for any of the circumstances in items (3) or (5) of the preceding paragraph, a fine of not less than 10,000 yuan but not more than 100,000 yuan shall be imposed; for the circumstance in item (6) of the preceding paragraph, a fine of not less than 30,000 yuan but not more than 300,000 yuan shall be imposed; for any of the circumstances in items (7) or (8) of the preceding paragraph, a fine of not less than 10,000 yuan but not more than 100,000 yuan shall be imposed, and if the circumstances are serious, a fine of not less than 100,000 yuan but not more than 500,000 yuan shall be imposed.

第一千一百五十五条 Any person who, in violation of this Law, commits any of the following acts shall be ordered to make corrections by the departments and agencies with the functions and duties of ecological and environmental protection supervision and management according to their respective functions and duties, and shall be fined:
(1) Engaging in the reception of ship pollutants and wastes, or ship tank cleaning and hold cleaning operations without having the corresponding reception and treatment capacity;
(2) A port, wharf, loading and unloading station, or shipbuilding, repairing, and scrapping unit fails to be equipped with or effectively operate facilities for receiving ship pollutants and wastes according to regulations;
(3) Engaging in ship scrapping, old ship conversion, salvage, or other above-water or underwater construction operations, causing marine environmental pollution damage;
(4) Carrying out ship scrapping operations on the coast by beaching.

For any of the circumstances in items (1) or (2) of the preceding paragraph, a fine of not less than 20,000 yuan but not more than 200,000 yuan shall be imposed; for the circumstance in item (3) of the preceding paragraph, a fine of not less than 50,000 yuan but not more than 200,000 yuan shall be imposed; for the circumstance in item (4) of the preceding paragraph, a fine of not less than 100,000 yuan but not more than 1,000,000 yuan shall be imposed.

第一千一百五十六条 Any person who, in violation of this Law, commits any of the following acts shall be ordered to make corrections by the departments and agencies with the functions and duties of ecological and environmental protection supervision and management according to their respective functions and duties, and shall be fined:
(1) Failing to declare or making false declarations regarding the advance declaration matters for a ship carrying pollution-hazardous goods;
(2) The shipper failing to truthfully inform the carrier of the proper name, pollution hazard, and the protective measures to be taken for the pollution-hazardous goods being shipped;
(3) The documents, packaging, marks, quantity restrictions, etc., of the pollution-hazardous goods delivered by the shipper to the carrier do not comply with the relevant regulations for the delivered goods;
(4) The shipper mixing pollution-hazardous goods into ordinary goods being shipped, or falsely declaring pollution-hazardous goods as ordinary goods;
(5) For goods with unknown pollution hazard that need to be carried by ship, failing to conduct an assessment in advance according to regulations.

For the circumstance in item (1) of the preceding paragraph, a fine of not less than 10,000 yuan but not more than 50,000 yuan shall be imposed; for any of the circumstances in items (3) or (5) of the preceding paragraph, a fine of not less than 20,000 yuan but not more than 100,000 yuan shall be imposed; for the circumstance in item (2) of the preceding paragraph, a fine of not less than 50,000 yuan but not more than 100,000 yuan shall be imposed; for the circumstance in item (4) of the preceding paragraph, a fine of not less than 100,000 yuan but not more than 200,000 yuan shall be imposed.

第一千一百五十九条 Any person who, in violation of this Law, commits any of the following acts shall be ordered to make corrections and be fined by the departments with the functions and duties of ecological and environmental protection supervision and management of the local people's government according to their respective functions and duties; if correction is refused, the person shall be ordered to restrict production or suspend production for remediation:
(1) A key unit for soil pollution supervision fails to establish and implement a system for investigating and rectifying soil and groundwater pollution hazards;
(2) A key unit for soil pollution supervision fails to formulate and implement a work plan for soil pollution prevention and control when dismantling facilities, equipment, or buildings or structures;
(3) When dismantling facilities, equipment, or buildings or structures, soil pollution prevention and control measures are not taken;
(4) The operation or management unit of a tailings pond fails to take effective measures to prevent soil pollution according to regulations, fails to take corresponding measures against risks and hazards, or the operation or management unit of a tailings pond that requires key supervision fails to monitor soil pollution conditions or conduct periodic assessments;
(5) In constructing and operating centralized sewage treatment facilities or solid waste disposal facilities, effective measures to prevent soil pollution are not taken in accordance with the requirements of laws, regulations, and relevant standards.

For any of the circumstances in the preceding paragraph, a fine of not less than 20,000 yuan but not more than 200,000 yuan shall be imposed; for any of the circumstances in items (2) to (5) of the preceding paragraph that causes serious consequences, a fine of not less than 200,000 yuan but not more than 2,000,000 yuan shall be imposed.

Article 1162 Where any entity, in violation of this Law, commits any of the following acts, the competent department of ecology and environment shall order rectification, confiscate illegal gains, and impose a fine of not less than RMB 100,000 yuan but not more than RMB 500,000 yuan; if the circumstances are serious, a fine of not less than RMB 500,000 yuan but not more than RMB 1,000,000 yuan shall be imposed concurrently; the directly responsible person in charge and other directly liable persons shall be fined not less than RMB 5,000 yuan but not more than RMB 20,000 yuan:
(1) Using resistance reduction products with heavy metal content exceeding the standard in soil;
(2) Failing to separately collect and store topsoil stripped during development and construction;
(3) Failing to take measures to treat or dispose of pollutants generated during risk control or remediation activities, or causing new pollution to soil or the surrounding environment;
(4) Where the transported contaminated soil is hazardous waste, the remediation construction unit fails to dispose of it according to law;
(5) Failing to report in advance the transportation time, method, route, quantity, destination and final disposal measures of contaminated soil to the competent department of ecology and environment of the location and the receiving place;
(6) Constructing a construction project that may cause soil pollution in the concentrated area of permanent basic farmland;
(7) Commencing construction of a project unrelated to risk control and remediation on a construction land plot that has not achieved the risk control and remediation objectives determined in the soil pollution risk assessment report, or has not conducted soil pollution status investigation, soil pollution risk assessment, risk control, remediation, effectiveness evaluation of risk control, or effectiveness evaluation of remediation as required.

Article 1165 Where the soil pollution liability entity or land use right holder, in violation of this Law, commits any of the following acts, the department responsible for ecological and environmental protection supervision and management of the local people's government shall, according to its duties, order rectification and impose a fine of not less than RMB 20,000 yuan but not more than RMB 200,000 yuan; if it refuses to rectify, a fine of not less than RMB 200,000 yuan but not more than RMB 1,000,000 yuan shall be imposed, and the performance shall be entrusted to another person, with the necessary expenses borne by the soil pollution liability entity or land use right holder; the directly responsible person in charge and other directly liable persons shall be fined not less than RMB 5,000 yuan but not more than RMB 20,000 yuan:
(1) Failing to conduct a soil pollution status investigation for construction land plots that, based on soil pollution status census, detailed survey, monitoring and on-site inspection, show risk of soil pollution, and plots whose use is changed to residential, public administration or public service land;
(2) Failing to conduct a soil pollution status investigation before the change of use of production and operation land of key soil pollution monitoring entities or before the withdrawal or transfer of land use rights;
(3) Failing to conduct soil pollution risk assessment for construction land plots, etc., whose soil pollution status investigation report evaluation shows that pollutant content exceeds the soil pollution risk control standard;
(4) Failing to take corresponding risk control measures for agricultural land plots in safe utilization and strict control categories, plots in the soil pollution risk control and remediation list of construction land, etc.;
(5) Failing to carry out remediation as required;
(6) Failing to entrust another relevant entity to evaluate the effectiveness of risk control and remediation after the completion of risk control and remediation activities.
If the soil pollution liability entity or land use right holder commits any of the circumstances in item (4) or (5) of the preceding paragraph and the circumstances are serious, the department responsible for ecological and environmental protection supervision and management shall transfer the case to the public security organ, which shall impose detention of not less than five days but not more than fifteen days on the directly responsible person in charge and other directly liable persons.

Article 1166 Where any entity, in violation of this Law, commits any of the following acts, the competent department of ecology and environment, the competent department of agriculture and rural affairs, or the competent department of forestry and grassland shall, according to their respective duties, order rectification; if it refuses to rectify, a fine of not less than RMB 20,000 yuan but not more than RMB 100,000 yuan shall be imposed:
(1) A key soil pollution monitoring entity fails to report the discharge of toxic and hazardous substances on an annual basis;
(2) A key soil pollution monitoring entity fails to report the information on underground storage tanks storing toxic and hazardous substances to the competent department of ecology and environment;
(3) The land use right holder fails to submit a soil pollution investigation report according to law;
(4) The soil pollution liability entity or land use right holder fails to submit a soil pollution risk assessment report according to law;
(5) The soil pollution liability entity fails to report risk control measures according to law;
(6) The soil pollution liability entity or land use right holder fails to file the remediation plan and effectiveness evaluation report according to law.

Article 1167 Where any entity, in violation of this Law, commits any of the following acts, the competent department of ecology and environment or the competent department of industry and information technology shall, according to their respective duties, order rectification; if it refuses to rectify, a fine of not less than RMB 10,000 yuan but not more than RMB 50,000 yuan shall be imposed:
(1) A key soil pollution monitoring entity fails to file a soil pollution prevention and control work plan;
(2) The land use right holder fails to file a soil pollution status investigation report.

Article 1171 Where any entity, in violation of this Law, commits any of the following acts, the competent department of ecology and environment shall order rectification, confiscate illegal gains, and impose a fine; if the circumstances are serious, submit to the people's government with approval authority for approval, and order suspension of business or closure:
(1) Constructing facilities and sites for centralized storage, utilization or disposal of industrial solid waste, construction waste, or hazardous waste, or domestic waste landfill sites, within ecological protection red line areas, concentrated areas of permanent basic farmland, or other areas requiring special protection;
(2) Transferring solid waste out of the administrative region of a province, autonomous region, or municipality directly under the Central Government for storage or disposal without approval;
(3) Transferring solid waste out of the administrative region of a province, autonomous region, or municipality directly under the Central Government for utilization without prior reporting of information;
(4) A unit that generates industrial solid waste, in violation of this Law, entrusts another person to transport, utilize or dispose of industrial solid waste;
(5) Failing to take protective measures that meet national ecological and environmental protection standards when storing industrial solid waste;
(6) A unit or other business operator violates other requirements for solid waste management, polluting the environment or damaging the ecology.
In the case of the circumstance in item (3) of the preceding paragraph, a fine of not less than RMB 50,000 yuan but not more than RMB 500,000 yuan shall be imposed; in the case of any circumstance other than item (3) of the preceding paragraph, a fine of not less than RMB 100,000 yuan but not more than RMB 1,000,000 yuan shall be imposed. Where punishment for the circumstance in item (6) of the preceding paragraph is otherwise provided by relevant laws or administrative regulations, such provisions shall apply.
Where any entity generating industrial solid waste, in violation of this Law, fails to establish an industrial solid waste management ledger and keep true records, the competent department of ecology and environment shall order rectification; if it refuses to rectify, a fine of not less than RMB 50,000 yuan but not more than RMB 200,000 yuan shall be imposed.

Article 1174 Where any entity, in violation of this Law, commits any of the following acts, the competent department of environmental sanitation shall order rectification, confiscate illegal gains, and impose a fine:
(1) Closing, leaving idle, or demolishing domestic waste treatment facilities or sites without authorization;
(2) A unit or other business operator that generates or collects kitchen waste fails to deliver the kitchen waste to a qualified entity for harmless treatment;
(3) A construction unit fails to utilize or dispose of construction waste generated during the construction process as required;
(4) A construction unit fails to prepare a construction waste treatment plan and file it, or fails to promptly remove construction waste generated during the construction process.
If a unit commits any of the circumstances in the preceding paragraph, a fine of not less than RMB 100,000 yuan but not more than RMB 1,000,000 yuan shall be imposed; if an individual commits the circumstance in item (2) of the preceding paragraph, a fine of not less than RMB 100 yuan but not more than RMB 500 yuan shall be imposed.
Where any entity, in violation of this Law, fails to sort and deposit domestic waste at the designated location, the competent department of environmental sanitation shall order rectification; if it refuses to rectify, a fine of not less than RMB 50,000 yuan but not more than RMB 500,000 yuan shall be imposed on the unit, and a fine according to law shall be imposed on the individual.

Article 1175 Where any entity, in violation of this Law, commits any of the following acts, the competent department of ecology and environment shall order rectification, confiscate illegal gains, and impose a fine; if the circumstances are serious, submit to the people's government with approval authority for approval, and order suspension of business or closure:
(1) Failing to set up hazardous waste identification signs;
(2) Failing to formulate a hazardous waste management plan, or failing to declare relevant information on hazardous waste;
(3) Failing to establish a hazardous waste management ledger and keep true records;
(4) Failing to store, utilize or dispose of hazardous waste in accordance with national regulations and ecological and environmental protection standards, or mixing hazardous waste with non-hazardous waste for storage;
(5) Providing or entrusting hazardous waste to an unlicensed unit or other business operator to engage in relevant activities;
(6) Mixing, collecting, storing, transporting or disposing of incompatible hazardous waste without safety treatment;
(7) Failing to fill in or run a hazardous waste transfer manifest;
(8) Transferring hazardous waste without authorization or approval;
(9) Transporting hazardous waste and passengers on the same means of transport;
(10) Without decontamination treatment, converting places, facilities, equipment, containers, packaging and other articles used for collecting, storing, transporting, utilizing or disposing of hazardous waste to other uses;
(11) Failing to formulate preventive measures and emergency plans for hazardous waste accidents.
In the case of any of the circumstances in items (1), (2), (3), (4), (6), (7), (9), (10) or (11) of the preceding paragraph, a fine of not less than RMB 50,000 yuan but not more than RMB 200,000 yuan shall be imposed; if the violator refuses to rectify, a fine of not less than RMB 200,000 yuan but not more than RMB 1,000,000 yuan shall be imposed; in the case of any of the circumstances in items (5) or (8) of the preceding paragraph, a fine of not less than RMB 200,000 yuan but not more than RMB 2,000,000 yuan shall be imposed.

Article 1179 Where any entity, in violation of this Law, commits any of the following acts, the public security organ shall impose detention of not less than 10 days but not more than 15 days on the legal representative, principal responsible person, directly responsible person in charge and other directly liable persons; if the circumstances are relatively minor, detention of not less than 5 days but not more than 10 days shall be imposed:
(1) Dumping, piling up, discarding, scattering, letting fall, or burning solid waste without authorization, causing serious consequences;
(2) Failing to take preventive measures, causing hazardous waste to scatter, run off, leak, or cause other serious consequences;
(3) Transferring hazardous waste without authorization or approval;
(4) Constructing facilities and sites for centralized storage, utilization or disposal of industrial solid waste, construction waste, or hazardous waste, or domestic waste landfill sites, within ecological protection red line areas, concentrated areas of permanent basic farmland, or other areas requiring special protection;
(5) Engaging in the business of collecting, storing, utilizing or disposing of hazardous waste without a license or in violation of the provisions of a license;
(6) Providing or entrusting hazardous waste to an unlicensed unit or individual to engage in relevant activities.

Article 1185: Where, in violation of the provisions of this Law, any construction entity or construction contractor falls under any of the following circumstances, the department designated by the local people's government at the project location shall order rectification and impose a fine of not less than RMB 10,000 but not more than RMB 100,000; if the violator refuses to rectify, it may order suspension of construction:
(1) Discharging construction noise exceeding the noise emission standards;
(2) Carrying out noise-generating construction operations at night in a concentrated area of noise-sensitive buildings without having obtained a certificate of continuous construction operations according to law.

Article 1186: Where, in violation of the provisions of this Law, any person falls under any of the following circumstances, the department designated by the local people's government at the project location shall order rectification and impose a fine of not less than RMB 5,000 but not more than RMB 50,000; if the violator refuses to rectify, a fine of not less than RMB 50,000 but not more than RMB 200,000 shall be imposed:
(1) The construction contractor fails to formulate an implementation plan for noise pollution prevention and control in accordance with the provisions, or fails to take effective measures to reduce vibration and noise;
(2) The construction entity fails to supervise the construction contractor in implementing the implementation plan for noise pollution prevention and control;
(3) The construction entity or construction contractor, having obtained the certificate of continuous construction operations according to law, fails to announce to nearby residents in accordance with the provisions.

Article 1188: Where, in violation of the provisions of this Law, any person falls under any of the following circumstances, the competent department of transport, the railway regulatory department, the competent department of civil aviation, or the relevant department of urban roads or urban rail transit designated by the local people's government shall, according to their respective functions and duties, order rectification and impose a fine of not less than RMB 5,000 but not more than RMB 50,000; if the violator refuses to rectify, a fine of not less than RMB 50,000 but not more than RMB 200,000 shall be imposed:
(1) The highway maintenance and management unit, urban road maintenance and repair unit, urban rail transit operation unit, or railway transport enterprise fails to fulfill the maintenance and repair obligations and fails to keep the vibration-reducing and noise-reducing facilities in normal operation;
(2) In constructing noise-sensitive buildings in a restricted construction area, the construction entity fails to carry out building sound insulation design or does not meet the requirements of the civil building acoustic design standards;
(3) The civil airport management organization, air transport enterprise, or general aviation enterprise fails to take measures to prevent or mitigate noise pollution from civil aircraft;
(4) The responsible enterprises or institutions fail to take effective measures to mitigate noise pollution in accordance with the requirements of the comprehensive noise pollution control plan.

Article 1189: Where, in violation of the provisions of this Law, any person falls under any of the following circumstances, the department designated by the local people's government shall order rectification and impose a fine of not less than RMB 5,000 but not more than RMB 50,000; if the violator refuses to rectify, a fine of not less than RMB 50,000 but not more than RMB 200,000 shall be imposed, and the violator may be ordered to suspend business upon approval by the people's government with the authority to approve:
(1) Discharging social life noise exceeding the noise emission standards;
(2) Using loudspeakers in commercial business activities or adopting other methods of continuously and repeatedly emitting high noise for advertising publicity;
(3) Failing to take effective measures to prevent other noise generated in commercial business activities, thereby causing noise pollution.

Article 1190: Where, in violation of the provisions of this Law, any person falls under any of the following circumstances, the department designated by the local people's government shall persuade and educate and order rectification; if the violator refuses to rectify, a warning shall be given, and a fine of not less than RMB 200 but not more than RMB 1,000 may be imposed on an individual, or a fine of not less than RMB 2,000 but not more than RMB 20,000 may be imposed on a unit:
(1) Using a loudspeaker in a concentrated area of noise-sensitive buildings;
(2) Organizing or engaging in recreational or fitness activities in public places, failing to comply with the provisions of the public place manager on activity areas, time periods, volume, etc., failing to take effective measures, thereby causing noise pollution, or using audio equipment in violation of the provisions, generating excessive volume;
(3) Carrying out interior decoration activities in a building that has been completed and delivered for use, not within the prescribed working hours, or failing to take effective measures, thereby causing noise pollution;
(4) Other acts in violation of laws and regulations that cause social life noise pollution.

Article 1196: Where, in violation of the provisions of this Law, any person falls under any of the following circumstances, the competent department of ecology and environment or the competent department of nuclear industry shall, according to their respective functions and duties, order rectification within a specified period and impose a fine of not less than RMB 20,000 but not more than RMB 200,000; if the violator fails to rectify within the specified period, the violator shall be ordered to restrict production or suspend production for remediation:
(1) Failing to set up radiation signs, warnings, and Chinese warning instructions in accordance with the provisions;
(2) Failing to establish and improve security protection systems in accordance with the provisions;
(3) Failing to store radioactive isotopes separately in accordance with the provisions;
(4) Failing to take safety and protection measures in accordance with the provisions;
(5) Failing to provide radiation safety education and training to its staff and take effective protection and safety measures.

Article 1199: Where, in violation of the provisions of this Law, any person falls under any of the following circumstances, the competent department of ecology and environment shall order cessation of the illegal act, order rectification within a specified period, and impose a fine of not less than RMB 50,000 but not more than RMB 500,000; if the violator fails to rectify within the specified period, the original licensing authority shall designate a unit with processing capability to carry out disposal or decommissioning on its behalf, with the costs borne by the unit that produced, sold, or used the radioactive isotopes or radiation devices:
(1) The unit producing radioactive sources or other producers or business operators fails to recover and reuse waste radioactive sources in accordance with the provisions;
(2) The unit using radioactive sources or other producers or business operators fails to return or deliver waste radioactive sources in accordance with the provisions;
(3) The premises using radioactive sources with a higher potential hazard to human health and the ecological environment, the premises producing radioactive isotopes, and the radiation devices that generate radioactive contamination after termination of operation fail to implement decommissioning according to law.

Article 1201. Where anyone, in violation of the provisions of this Law, falls under any of the following circumstances, the competent department of ecological environment shall order the cessation of the illegal act, set a deadline for correction, and impose a fine:
(1) entities that produce or use radioisotopes and radiation devices and other producers and business operators fail to collect, package, and store the radioactive waste generated according to the provisions;
(2) failing to construct facilities such as tailings ponds, or constructing facilities such as tailings ponds that do not meet the requirements for prevention and control of radioactive pollution to store and dispose of radioactive solid waste such as tailings from uranium (thorium) mines and associated radioactive mines;
(3) failing to treat or store radioactive liquid waste that shall not be discharged into the environment according to the provisions;
(4) discharging radioactive liquid waste not in the manner prescribed;
(5) providing or entrusting radioactive waste to entities or individuals without a license for storage, treatment, and disposal.
For any of the circumstances under subparagraph (1) or (3) of the preceding paragraph, a fine of not less than RMB 50,000 but not more than RMB 500,000 shall be imposed; for any of the circumstances under subparagraph (2), (4), or (5) of the preceding paragraph, a fine of not less than RMB 100,000 but not more than RMB 1,000,000 shall be imposed.

Article 1208. Where an enterprise or institution that is not subject to pollutant discharge permit management, in violation of the provisions of this Law, falls under any of the following circumstances, the departments and agencies responsible for ecological and environmental protection supervision and management shall, in accordance with their respective functions and duties, order correction and impose a fine of not less than RMB 20,000 but not more than RMB 200,000; if correction is refused, restricted production or suspension of production for remediation may be ordered:
(1) discharging electromagnetic radiation that exceeds the emission standards for electromagnetic radiation;
(2) failing to take measures for prevention and control of electromagnetic radiation pollution to prevent or mitigate electromagnetic radiation pollution according to law.

Article 1217. Where anyone, in violation of the provisions of this Law concerning marine ecological protection, falls under any of the following circumstances, the departments and agencies responsible for ecological and environmental protection supervision and management shall, in accordance with their respective functions and duties, order correction and impose a fine:
(1) occupying or damaging natural shorelines;
(2) mining sea sand within the scope of strictly protected shorelines;
(3) developing and utilizing sea sand resources in areas other than the scope of strictly protected shorelines, without taking strict measures to protect marine ecology according to law;
(4) a sea sand miner fails to provide a legal source certificate for a vessel carrying sea sand according to law;
(5) transporting sea sand resources without holding a legal source certificate.
For the circumstance under subparagraph (1) of the preceding paragraph, a fine of not less than RMB 500 but not more than RMB 10,000 per meter shall be imposed; for the circumstance under subparagraph (2) of the preceding paragraph, a fine of not less than two times but not more than twenty times the value of the goods shall be imposed, and if the value of the goods is less than RMB 100,000, a fine of not less than RMB 200,000 but not more than RMB 2,000,000 shall be imposed; for any of the circumstances under subparagraph (3), (4), or (5) of the preceding paragraph, a fine of not less than RMB 50,000 but not more than RMB 500,000 shall be imposed.
